In this code block, the assertion is checking if the ArrayList's capacity has been changed during the execution of the Add method. ArrayList's Add method increases the capacity when the list becomes full, which means it will reallocate the internal array to a larger size if the Count (which is the same as the size of the list) reaches the current Capacity. The assertion checks if the new capacity is the same as the old capacity which would mean that the list has successfully increased its capacity without any errors. The 'RET' in the assertion refers to the return value of the Add method.
--------------------
Debug.Assert(COUNT(RET) == COUNT(_items) - 1);
</code>

The given C# code snippet has a comment that starts with "@@@", which says "@@@ COUNT should be one less than the capacity of the array after the element is added". Here, COUNT(RET) refers to the new count returned by the Add method after the element is added, and COUNT(_items) - 1 refers to the new capacity of the array after the element is added. So, the assertion is ensuring that COUNT(RET) is exactly one less than the capacity of the array after the element is added.
